["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Your Tikka already shoots better than most new hunters can. Money spent on glass, practice and a few simple tools beats money spent on parts.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 382\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Upgrades for the Arctic. Worth it, in order: 1 scope, rings and a torque driver, in orange; 2 snap caps and a cleaning kit; 3 shooting sticks; 4 a sling; 5 a spare magazine. Not worth it yet: 6 an aftermarket trigger, yours is good; 7 a muzzle brake, loud and it replaces the front sight; 8 a new stock or chassis. Never, illegal in Canada: a suppressor, or cutting the barrel or stock short.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"382\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Upgrades: worth it, or not</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"150\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Worth it, in this order</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"84\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Scope, rings, torque driver</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"106\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Snap caps and a cleaning kit</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"128\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shooting sticks</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"150\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sling</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"172\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Spare magazine</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"200\" width=\"376\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Not worth it yet</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"242\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Aftermarket trigger: yours is good</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"264\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">7</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Muzzle brake: loud, loses the front sight</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"286\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">8</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">New stock or chassis: learn this one</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"312\" width=\"376\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"334\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Never: illegal in Canada</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"356\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Suppressor. Cutting the barrel or stock short.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Worth it: scope and rings, practice tools, sticks, sling (Tip).</li><li>Never: a suppressor or a shortened barrel <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>What to buy first and why, prices in three tiers, the legal lines, length of pull spacers, the oversized bolt knob, and what to skip.</li><li>Budget: your gear budget is about $10,000 in total (owner, prompt 2026-10-23). A full rifle setup below fits in about $1,500 to $3,500 (Tip, from the prices in this chapter).</li><li>Previous: <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-08\">Cold and wet care</a>. Next: <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-10\">Range day plan</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 382\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Upgrades for the Arctic. Worth it, in order: 1 scope, rings and a torque driver, in orange; 2 snap caps and a cleaning kit; 3 shooting sticks; 4 a sling; 5 a spare magazine. Not worth it yet: 6 an aftermarket trigger, yours is good; 7 a muzzle brake, loud and it replaces the front sight; 8 a new stock or chassis. Never, illegal in Canada: a suppressor, or cutting the barrel or stock short.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"382\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Upgrades: worth it, or not</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"150\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Worth it, in this order</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"84\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Scope, rings, torque driver</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"106\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Snap caps and a cleaning kit</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"128\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shooting sticks</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"150\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sling</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"172\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Spare magazine</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"200\" width=\"376\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Not worth it yet</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"242\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Aftermarket trigger: yours is good</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"264\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">7</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Muzzle brake: loud, loses the front sight</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"286\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">8</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">New stock or chassis: learn this one</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"312\" width=\"376\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"334\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Never: illegal in Canada</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"356\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Suppressor. Cutting the barrel or stock short.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>1 Scope, rings and a torque driver (Tip).</li><li>2 Snap caps and a cleaning kit (95%, the manual asks for both).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why each one, with my reasons</summary><ol><li><strong>Scope, rings, torque driver:</strong> the biggest gain in dawn light and at 150 m plus (Tip). <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-04\">Chapter 4</a>.</li><li><strong>Snap caps and a cleaning kit:</strong> the manual recommends snap caps for dry fire and lists the cleaning kit (95%, Tikka manual pages 9 and 18). Cheap and used every week.</li><li><strong>Shooting sticks:</strong> most Fraser Valley shots will be sitting or standing, not prone (Tip). Sticks make those steady.</li><li><strong>Sling:</strong> carry hands free on long walks and a steadier hasty sling position (Tip; see <a href=\"#/s/field-positions/0\">field positions</a>). Your rifle has standard sling studs front and rear (95%, page 16).</li><li><strong>Spare magazine:</strong> a second loaded magazine in a pocket, and a spare if one is lost (Tip). Use only a magazine made for your Tikka (Tip; the manual recommends original parts, 95%).</li><li>Bipod: useful prone or on a bench; heavy and slow in timber. The front stud takes one (95%, page 16). My lean: sticks first, bipod later.</li></ol></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 360\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gear prices in Canadian dollars, three tiers, price checked 23 October 2026 from search previews: scope entry $400, mid $840, premium $1,700 and up; rings $35, $120, $260; shooting sticks entry $130, other tiers to verify; bipod entry $140, others to verify; a spare Tikka 10 round magazine about $220; .308 snap caps about 30 US dollars for 10.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"360\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gear prices, three tiers (CAD)</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Item</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Entry</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Mid</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"62\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Premium</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"72\" width=\"376\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"92\" font-si