D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Magazine</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">$220</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><text x=\"320\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"252\" width=\"376\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"16\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Snap caps</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">US$30</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><text x=\"320\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\"></text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"296\" width=\"376\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Price checked 2026-10-23, search</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"336\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">previews. Check at the till.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>CAD (Canadian dollars), price checked 2026-10-23 (55 to 65%).</li><li>Blank or <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>: no Canadian price found today.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every price and its source</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Entry</th><th>Mid</th><th>Premium</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Scope</td><td>Vortex Diamondback 3 to 9x40 $399.99</td><td>Leupold VX 3HD 3.5 to 10x40 $839.99</td><td>Leupold VX 5HD 3 to 15x44 $1,700 to $2,500</td><td>(55 to 65%)</td></tr><tr><td>Rings</td><td>Leupold Rifleman 1 in $34</td><td>Vortex Pro 30 mm $119 to $130</td><td>Nightforce Ultralite 30 mm $236 to $264</td><td>(65%, scope guide 2026-10-01)</td></tr><tr><td>Shooting sticks</td><td>Primos Trigger Stick bipod $129.77 at Cabela's Canada</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Bipod</td><td>Harris BRM 6 to 9 in $139.99 at Rangeview Sports</td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td><span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Spare magazine</td><td>Tikka CTR, Arctic, TAC A1 10 round, .308: $219.99 at Rangeview Sports</td><td></td><td></td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Snap caps .308</td><td>A Zoom 10 pack about US$29 to $34; CAD <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td></td><td></td><td><span class=\"cert c-tip\" title=\"Certainty\">55%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Torque driver</td><td>Wheeler FAT Wrench about US$75; CAD <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span></td><td></td><td></td><td><span class=\"cert c-tip\" title=\"Certainty\">55%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Search previews of Canadian shops, 2026-10-23. Stock and prices change; check at the till.</li><li>Oversized Tikka bolt knob: price <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> at a Tikka dealer.</li><li>Cleaning kit (rod, guide, brushes, solvent, CLP): <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>. Buy a one piece coated rod and a bore guide that fits the Tikka action (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 382\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Upgrades for the Arctic. Worth it, in order: 1 scope, rings and a torque driver, in orange; 2 snap caps and a cleaning kit; 3 shooting sticks; 4 a sling; 5 a spare magazine. Not worth it yet: 6 an aftermarket trigger, yours is good; 7 a muzzle brake, loud and it replaces the front sight; 8 a new stock or chassis. Never, illegal in Canada: a suppressor, or cutting the barrel or stock short.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"382\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Upgrades: worth it, or not</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"150\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Worth it, in this order</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"84\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Scope, rings, torque driver</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"106\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Snap caps and a cleaning kit</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"128\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"133\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Shooting sticks</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"150\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Sling</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"172\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Spare magazine</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"200\" width=\"376\" height=\"104\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Not worth it yet</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"242\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Aftermarket trigger: yours is good</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"264\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">7</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Muzzle brake: loud, loses the front sight</text><circle cx=\"34\" cy=\"286\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"34\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">8</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">New stock or chassis: learn this one</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"312\" width=\"376\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"334\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Never: illegal in Canada</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"356\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Suppressor. Cutting the barrel or stock short.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The factory trigger is good. Leave it <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>A muzzle brake replaces your front sight and adds noise <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why to wait</summary><ul><li><strong>Aftermarket trigger:</strong> Tikka says the action's precision parts \"should not be altered, modified or changed\" and that a replaced trigger, sear or safety needs the trigger returned to the maker (95%, Tikka manual page 15). Using parts that are not Sako or Tikka can cause malfunctions not covered by the warranty (95%, page 4).</li><li><strong>Muzzle brake:</strong> the Arctic front sight sits on the muzzle thread (95%, page 11). Recoil's reviewers noted they could not fit a brake \"without losing the front sight\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Brakes are louder for you and your partner (Tip). Thread size on your rifle: 5/8 x 24 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li><strong>New stock or chassis:</strong> the laminate stock is stable in wet weather (Tip). Learn this one first.</li><li><strong>Bigger scope:</strong> 15x or more is heavier and darker at dusk for close black tails (Tip).</li><li><strong>Hand loading:</strong> voids the Tikka warranty (95%, page 9).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 392\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The legal lines for changes to your rifle: 1 a suppressor or silencer is a prohibited device; 2 a barrel cut under 457 mm and 3 a whole rifle cut under 660 mm make a prohibited firearm; 4 a semi automatic rifle magazine over 5 rounds is a prohibited device; 5 a muzzle brake is not named in section 84; 6 a scope, sling and sticks are fine. Unsure: ask a qualified gunsmith first.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"392\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The legal lines</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"64\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Suppressor or silencer</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited device</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"92\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"114\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Barrel cut under 457 mm</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited firearm</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"142\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"164\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Whole rifle under 660 mm</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"179\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited firearm</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"192\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"214\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"219\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"211\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Semi auto magazine over 5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"229\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited device</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"242\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"264\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Muzzle brake</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">not named in s. 84</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"292\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"314\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"319\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"311\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Scope, sling, sticks</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"329\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">fine</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"346\" width=\"376\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"368\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unsure? Ask a qualified gunsmith first.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A suppressor is a prohibited device in Canada <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Never shorten the barrel or stock <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the law</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>\"prohibited device means ... (c) a device or contrivance designed or intended to muffle or stop the sound or report of a firearm\"</p></aside><ul><li>Source: Criminal Code s. 84(1), current to 30 September 2026, read 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. The Tikka manual covers suppressor fitting because some countries allow them; it also says follow national law (95%, page 17).</li><li>Cutting a rifle so it is under 660 mm long, or its barrel under 457 mm: a prohibited firearm (99%, s. 84(1)). Chapter 1 has the full text.</li><li>Magazines: the 5 round limit is for magazines designed for semi automatic firearms (99%, SOR/98-462 Part 4 s. 3). Never alter a magazine (Tip). Chapter 2.</li><li>Muzzle brakes are not named in s. 84 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Ask the store and a qualified gunsmith before fitting one (Tip).</li><li>Anything that changes how the action works, its barrel length, or its magazine: ask a qualified gunsmith first. Never alter a gun in a way that could change its legal class (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 386\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Length of pull spacers: 1 spacers stack between the stock and the recoil pad; 2, in orange, more than two spacers need longer screws; 3 the recoil pad, do not overtighten its screws. A little soapy water around the pad screw holes stops the pad tearing.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"386\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Length of pull: spacers</text><path d=\"M60 70 L240 60 L240 200 L60 210Z\" fill=\"#C29A66\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><rect x=\"242\" y=\"60\" width=\"12\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><rect x=\"258\" y=\"60\" width=\"12\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#8F9A8C\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><path d=\"M276 60 L300 58 Q310 130 300 202 L276 200Z\" fill=\"#3A463C\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"96\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"240\" y1=\"164\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"164\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"254\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"254\" cy=\"190\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"236\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><line x1=\"340\" y1=\"70\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"96\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"96\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"70\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><line x1=\"340\" y1=\"236\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"190\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><circle cx=\"290\" cy=\"190\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"236\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"241\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"265\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Spacers between stock and pad</text><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"287\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Over 2 spacers: longer screws</text><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"309\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Recoil pad. Do not overtighten</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"340\" width=\"376\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Soapy water on the pad screw holes.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Spacers set length of pull. Over 2 need longer screws <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>An oversized bolt knob helps with gloves <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the manual's steps</summary><ul><li>Length of pull (95%, Tikka manual page 15): loosen the two recoil pad screws (soapy water around the pad screw holes stops tearing), add or remove spacers, tighten the screws. \"Should you need to stack more than two spacers, you will need to replace the recoil screws with longer ones.\"</li><li>\"Make sure to use screws of appropriate length and do not overtighten them. In other case the stock may be damaged beyond repair\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>The Arctic came with 3 light metal spacers in the box (75%, all4shooters). Check your box.</li><li>Fit test (Tip): rifle mounted in your hunting jacket, your nose about two fingers behind your thumb on the grip. Winter jacket means fewer spacers.</li><li>Oversized bolt knob: push it over the original knob and tighten the screw inside it, 5 to 10 turns, holding the knob still (95%, page 17).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 392\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The legal lines for changes to your rifle: 1 a suppressor or silencer is a prohibited device; 2 a barrel cut under 457 mm and 3 a whole rifle cut under 660 mm make a prohibited firearm; 4 a semi automatic rifle magazine over 5 rounds is a prohibited device; 5 a muzzle brake is not named in section 84; 6 a scope, sling and sticks are fine. Unsure: ask a qualified gunsmith first.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"392\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The legal lines</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"42\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"64\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">1</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"61\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Suppressor or silencer</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited device</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"92\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"114\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"119\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">2</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Barrel cut under 457 mm</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"129\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited firearm</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"142\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"164\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">3</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"161\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Whole rifle under 660 mm</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"179\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited firearm</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"192\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFE6D6\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"214\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"219\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">4</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"211\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Semi auto magazine over 5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"229\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">prohibited device</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"242\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"264\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">5</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"261\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Muzzle brake</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"279\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">not named in s. 84</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"292\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"32\" cy=\"314\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"319\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"311\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Scope, sling, sticks</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"329\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"start\">fine</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"346\" width=\"376\" height=\"34\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#DCE3D6\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"368\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unsure? Ask a qualified gunsmith first.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>\"Glass, practice, then parts.\"</strong></li><li><strong>\"Can is a crime.\"</strong> A suppressor is a prohibited device in Canada.</li><li><strong>\"Two spacers, short screws; three, long screws.\"</strong></li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: mistakes, rule and the field task</summary><ul><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (opinion): \"Buy ammunition before accessories.\"</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Buying a trigger kit before a box of practice ammunition.</li><li>Ordering a suppressor online from a US site. It is prohibited here.</li><li>Over tightening the recoil pad screws and cracking the stock.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Write your shopping list in the order on this page, with a price checked date. Buy the first two items before the next range day.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>Tikka manual <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Criminal Code and SOR/98-462 read directly <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Prices: search previews (55 to 65%). Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://media.sako.global/image/upload/v1691658741/Tikka_T1x_T3x_Instruction_Manual_v5.3_cjggnu.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Tikka T1x and T3x instruction manual v5.3 (PDF)</a>: original parts (page 4), ammunition (page 9), Arctic sights (page 11), trigger (page 15), length of pull (page 15), sling studs (page 16), suppressor note (page 17), oversized bolt knob (page 17), cleaning kit (page 18). Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/C-46/section-84.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Criminal Code s. 84</a> and <a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-98-462/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOR/98-462</a>, current to 30 September 2026. Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.recoilweb.com/tikka-t3x-arctic-131608.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Recoil review</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span> and <a href=\"https://www.all4shooters.com/en/hunting/rifles/tikka-t3x-arctic-bolt-action-in-308-winchester-features-test/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">all4shooters test</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>, read 2026-10-23</li><li>Prices, search previews 2026-10-23: <a href=\"https://cabelas.ca/product/61470\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cabela's Canada Primos Trigger Stick</a>, <a href=\"https://rangeviewsports.ca/product/harris-engineering-series-1a2-model-brm-bipod\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rangeview Harris BRM</a>, <a href=\"https://www.rangeviewsports.ca/?p=194953\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rangeview Tikka magazine</a>, <a href=\"https://palmettostatearmory.com/a-zoom-aluminum-value-pack-snap-cap-308-win-10-pack-12328.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Palmetto State Armory A Zoom .308</a>, <a href=\"https://www.pelicansalessupply.com/products/wheeler-2023-fat-wrench-black\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Pelican Sales Wheeler FAT Wrench</a>; scope and ring prices as in <a href=\"#/s/mc-tikka-04\">chapter 4</a> and the <a href=\"#/s/scope-guide/0\">scope guide</a> (55 to 65%)</li></ul></details>"]